# Developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true. Without this file the tree
# drifted: deploy.sh was LF, package.sh CRLF, and every `git add` of a
# newly written file printed a line-ending warning.

# Normalise to LF in the repository; Windows working copies still get CRLF
# for ordinary text, which is what the C# tooling here expects.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts are the exception that made this file necessary: Git Bash
# runs them as-is, and a CRLF script fails on the stray carriage return.
# These stay LF in the working tree on every platform.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Never touch binaries. icon.png in particular -- a line-ending conversion
# applied to a PNG corrupts it silently, and Thunderstore rejects the
# package rather than explaining why.
*.png binary
*.dll binary
*.zip binary
*.unity3d binary
